      "updated": 1780851840571,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\n1) Functional Requirements:  \n- Artists should be able to upload songs.\n- Users should be able to search and stream songs.\n- Users should be able to create and manage playlists (add/remove\nsongs).\n- Users should be able to maintain profiles.\n- Users should be able to like/unlike songs and follow artists.\n\n---- Out of scope ------\n- recommendation engine and discover weekly generation.\n- protection against copyrighted or bad content.\n\n\n2) Scale of the System: \n- Total Active Users (MAU): ~750M\n- Daily Active Users (DAU): ~250M\n- Total Song Catalog: ~100M songs\n- Daily Streams: ~5B (assuming ~20 songs/user/day)\n- Daily Song Uploads: ~60k tracks/day\n\n3) Non Functional Requirements (SPARCS):  \n- Scalability: System must handle 5B streams/day and immense global\nconcurrent traffic.\n- Performance: Low latency streaming with fast playback start times;\nminimal rebuffering.\n- Availability: Highly available architecture via CDNs to stream audio\nglobally without disruption.\n- Reliability: Adaptive quality switching (e.g., 64kbps, 128kbps, 320kbps\nOgg/AAC formats).\n\n4) BOE Calculations: \n- Load / Traffic (QPS)\n    > Read QPS: (5B)/ (10^5) => 50k QPS\n    > Write QPS: 60k/(10^5) = 0.6 QPS\n    > Peak QPS: (X3) ≈ 150k QPS\n\n- Storage\n    > Daily storage = 60k writes × 3MB average request => 180 GB\n    > Yearly storage = 80 GB × 365 => 65 TB\n    > Total storage = 300 TB + (65 TB × 5) => 625 TB\n    > replication ≈ 625 TB × 3 => 1,875 TB (1.87 PB)\n\n- Bandwidth\n    > Ingress = 0.6 write QPS × 3MB => 1.8 MB/s\n    > Egress = 50,000 read QPS × 3MB => 150,000 MB/s (150 GB/s)\n\n- Cache \n    > 5B*3MB*0.2 => 3PB\n\n5) Core Entities \n- User: UserID, Email, SubscriptionType\n- Artist: ArtistID, Name\n- Song: SongID, Title, Duration, FileURL, ArtistID\n- Playlist: PlaylistID, OwnerID, Name\n- PlaylistItem: PlaylistID, SongID, Position\n\n\n6) API Design \n\n> Search & Discovery\nGET /search?q={query}&type=song,artist&limit=20&offset=0\n    Output: 2xx, {results}\n\nGET /songs/trending?genre={genre}&limit=50\n    Output: 2xx, {trending_songs}\n\nGET /artists/{id}/songs?limit=50\n    Output: 2xx, {artist_songs}\n\n> Content Access\nGET /songs/{id}\n    Output: 2xx, {song_metadata, streaming_url}\n\nGET /songs/{id}/stream\n    Output: 2xx, Direct streaming endpoint\n\nGET /playlists/{id}?include_songs=true\n    Output: 2xx, {playlist_details, songs: []}\n\n> User Actions\nPOST /playlists\n    Input: {\"name\": \"My Favorites\", \"is_public\": false}\n    Output: 2xx, success\n\nPUT /playlists/{id}/songs\n    Input: {\"song_ids\": [123, 456], \"position\": 5}\n    Output: 2xx, success\n\nDELETE /playlists/{id}/songs/{song_id}\n    Output: 2xx, success\n\nPOST /songs/{id}/like\n    Output: 2xx, success\n    User Management\n\nGET /users/me/playlists\n    Output: 2xx, {user_playlists}\n\nGET /users/me/liked-songs?limit=50&offset=0\n    Output: 2xx, {liked_songs}\n\nPOST /users/me/follow/{artist_id}\n    Output: 2xx, success\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\n1) Functional Requirements:  \n- Artists should be able to upload songs.\n- Users should be able to search and stream songs.\n- Users should be able to create and manage playlists (add/remove songs).\n- Users should be able to maintain profiles.\n- Users should be able to like/unlike songs and follow artists.\n\n---- Out of scope ------\n- recommendation engine and discover weekly generation.\n- protection against copyrighted or bad content.\n\n\n2) Scale of the System: \n- Total Active Users (MAU): ~750M\n- Daily Active Users (DAU): ~250M\n- Total Song Catalog: ~100M songs\n- Daily Streams: ~5B (assuming ~20 songs/user/day)\n- Daily Song Uploads: ~60k tracks/day\n\n3) Non Functional Requirements (SPARCS):  \n- Scalability: System must handle 5B streams/day and immense global concurrent traffic.\n- Performance: Low latency streaming with fast playback start times; minimal rebuffering.\n- Availability: Highly available architecture via CDNs to stream audio globally without disruption.\n- Reliability: Adaptive quality switching (e.g., 64kbps, 128kbps, 320kbps Ogg/AAC formats).\n\n4) BOE Calculations: \n- Load / Traffic (QPS)\n    > Read QPS: (5B)/ (10^5) => 50k QPS\n    > Write QPS: 60k/(10^5) = 0.6 QPS\n    > Peak QPS: (X3) ≈ 150k QPS\n\n- Storage\n    > Daily storage = 60k writes × 3MB average request => 180 GB\n    > Yearly storage = 80 GB × 365 => 65 TB\n    > Total storage = 300 TB + (65 TB × 5) => 625 TB\n    > replication ≈ 625 TB × 3 => 1,875 TB (1.87 PB)\n\n- Bandwidth\n    > Ingress = 0.6 write QPS × 3MB => 1.8 MB/s\n    > Egress = 50,000 read QPS × 3MB => 150,000 MB/s (150 GB/s)\n\n- Cache \n    > 5B*3MB*0.2 => 3PB\n\n5) Core Entities \n- User: UserID, Email, SubscriptionType\n- Artist: ArtistID, Name\n- Song: SongID, Title, Duration, FileURL, ArtistID\n- Playlist: PlaylistID, OwnerID, Name\n- PlaylistItem: PlaylistID, SongID, Position\n\n\n6) API Design \n\n> Search & Discovery\nGET /search?q={query}&type=song,artist&limit=20&offset=0\n    Output: 2xx, {results}\n\nGET /songs/trending?genre={genre}&limit=50\n    Output: 2xx, {trending_songs}\n\nGET /artists/{id}/songs?limit=50\n    Output: 2xx, {artist_songs}\n\n> Content Access\nGET /songs/{id}\n    Output: 2xx, {song_metadata, streaming_url}\n\nGET /songs/{id}/stream\n    Output: 2xx, Direct streaming endpoint\n\nGET /playlists/{id}?include_songs=true\n    Output: 2xx, {playlist_details, songs: []}\n\n> User Actions\nPOST /playlists\n    Input: {\"name\": \"My Favorites\", \"is_public\": false}\n    Output: 2xx, success\n\nPUT /playlists/{id}/songs\n    Input: {\"song_ids\": [123, 456], \"position\": 5}\n    Output: 2xx, success\n\nDELETE /playlists/{id}/songs/{song_id}\n    Output: 2xx, success\n\nPOST /songs/{id}/like\n    Output: 2xx, success\n    User Management\n\nGET /users/me/playlists\n    Output: 2xx, {user_playlists}\n\nGET /users/me/liked-songs?limit=50&offset=0\n    Output: 2xx, {liked_songs}\n\nPOST /users/me/follow/{artist_id}\n    Output: 2xx, success\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
